    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{12}{35}$, assuming the events are independent.",
      "worked": "Assuming sleeping through the alarm and bus lateness are independent:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{bus not late})&=1-\\frac{3}{7}\\\\P(\\text{bus not late})&=\\frac{4}{7}\\\\P(\\text{sleep through alarm and bus not late})&=\\frac{3}{5}\\times\\frac{4}{7}\\\\P(\\text{sleep through alarm and bus not late})&=\\frac{12}{35}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
